      en: "Mamba Point Cliff is a coastal landmark that defines Monrovia's shoreline. The cliff provides natural protection against storm surges. It is underlain by sedimentary layers containing fossilized shells. The site is popular for photography and leisure. However, unregulated construction has increased erosion risks. The Monrovia city government has initiated cliff stabilization projects. The area also hosts a historic lighthouse built in 1920.",
